@startuml E01-back-referral-gap
!theme plain
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

title E-01 — The Back-Referral Black Hole\nConsultation summary stranded on the receiving side

rectangle "Initiating Facility" #FFF9C4 {
  component "DR. SANTOS\n(referring)" as santos
  component "Patient Record\n(PHC system)" as phrec
  component "eReferral Module\n(Task requester)" as eref_init
}

rectangle "Shared FHIR Server / Receiving Facility" #FFE0CC {
  component "Task/close-004\nstatus = completed\noutput[0].type = #consultation-summary\noutput[0].value = 'Ultrasound 18wks:\nSingle viable fetus.\nPlacenta posterior, no praevia.\nFHR 152 bpm.\nFollow-up ANC in 4 weeks.'" as task
  component "ERefServiceRequest/mat-004\nstatus = active" as sr
}

rectangle "What is NOT in the IG" #FFCCCC {
  component "FHIR Subscription\n(push notification)" as sub #FFAAAA
  component "Back-referral Task\n(direction: receiving → initiating)" as backtask #FFAAAA
  component "Communication Resource\n(from receiving to referring)" as comm #FFAAAA
  component "Polling SLA\n(how often, by whom?)" as poll #FFAAAA
}

santos     --> eref_init : Creates referral
eref_init  --> sr        : POST ServiceRequest
eref_init  --> task      : POST Task (status=requested)

task       -[dashed]-> task : [receiving facility updates:\nstatus=received → accepted → completed]

task       -[dashed,#red]-> santos  : ❌ No notification path
task       -[dashed,#red]-> phrec   : ❌ No update to patient record
task       -[dashed,#red]-> sub     : ❌ Not defined in IG
task       -[dashed,#red]-> backtask: ❌ No back-referral resource
task       -[dashed,#red]-> comm    : ❌ Communication not in scope
task       -[dashed,#red]-> poll    : ❌ No polling requirement

note bottom
  After the referral completes, DR. SANTOS:
  - Does not receive the consultation summary
  - Does not know the outcome unless polling GET Task?requester=...
  - Cannot update the patient's PHC record automatically
  - Cannot schedule the follow-up ANC contact based on the summary

  The patient must relay the findings verbally at the next visit.
  If the patient does not attend, the primary care record is never updated.

  This is the second half of a referral conversation that is not modelled.
end note

@enduml
